00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.880
Rhiannon: Mental health issues in
children are generally defined as

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.320
delays or disruptions in development,
related to age-appropriate thinking,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.209
behaviours, social skills or
regulation of their emotions.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.070
Leah: These problems are distressing
to children and disrupt their ability

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.630
to function well in the home, in
school or in other social interactions.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.210
It can be difficult to understand mental
health issues in children because normal

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.800
childhood development is a process
that involves all kinds of changes.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:32.119
Rhiannon: Mental health concerns
may also differ depending on a

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.080
child's age, as they may not been
able to explain how they feel, or

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.210
why they are behaving a certain way.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.820
Leah: If a child or young person’s
behaviour is a cause for concern it

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.919
should not be ignored, but should be
addressed either by trying to talk

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.790
to them, or those that know them best
and getting the support of a doctor.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:52.050
Rhiannon: Once the problem has
been identified it is easier

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.469
to try to find a solution.

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:55.820
Let’s hear from someone who
can tell us more about this.

